<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23466" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δᾱρεικός</span></b> , ὁ, a
		Persian gold coin (but <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δ. ἀργύρειοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Cim.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			),  prop. Adj. agreeing with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στατήρ</span> (in full, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				8.28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.28
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				602
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				1.1.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				7.122
			</span></i>, etc.; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσὸς χαρακτῆρα Δαρεικὸν ἔχων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					17.66
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσὸς Δαρεικός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					1.5
				</span></i>
			:—written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαρικός</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαριχός</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(1).1
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Sparta</span>). (From <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαρεῖος,</span> cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				3.87
			</span></i>, acc. to some not <i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i> Nothus, <i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i>; the connection with Bab. <i>dariku</i> (dub. sens.) is
				v. doubtful.)</div>
